{% set local_problem %}
<p>Owens Cross Roads' terrain is both a challenge and an opportunity for drainage. Water runs downhill — so on sloped properties, gravity can do most of the work moving water away from your foundation. The key is capturing that water and directing it through proper channels.</p>

<p>Surface drainage has limits. Splash blocks move water only a few feet. Above-ground extensions get damaged by mowers and look unsightly. During heavy storms, surface discharge can't keep up with the volume.</p>

<p>Underground drains solve all of this. They capture water at each downspout and carry it through buried pipes to a safe discharge point — using your terrain's natural slope to move water 20, 30, even 50+ feet from your foundation.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains include catch basins at each downspout, solid PVC pipe buried underground with proper slope, and discharge points at safe locations away from structures.</p>

<p>We assess your property's terrain, identify optimal discharge locations, and design a system that uses gravity effectively.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed underground drainage on properties throughout Owens Cross Roads and know how to work with the area's variable terrain. Based just 16 miles away, we stand behind our work.</p>
{% endset %}

